  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At Port Santa Lucia in Saint-Raphaël, Le Pescadou serves traditional Mediterranean cuisine made with fresh, local produce — fresh seafood, generous portions praised in reviews — in a warm décor extended by a terrace overlooking the harbour. Two consistent platforms give it an excellent rating: 4.8/5 (280+ reviews) and 4.9/5 on Restaurant Guru (848 reviews). The menu changes every day apart from two signature dishes, and there is a rooftop and a cocktail bar.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's page on the Saint-Raphaël tourist office website, repeated by the Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur regional tourist board and Esterel Côte d'Azur, lists "Pets welcome" among its services. No condition is given (lead, size, indoor or terrace), and the restaurant's own website does not mention dogs. The dining room seats 90, including 50 on a shaded terrace. For the 2026 season (5 January to 30 November) the tourist office gives opening hours of 11:30-15:00 and 19:00-23:00 on Monday, Thursday, Friday and weekends, 11:30-15:00 on Tuesday, and closed on Wednesday.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask directly for a terrace table on arrival, that's where the Port Santa Lucia atmosphere is best enjoyed with your dog at your feet.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Port Santa Lucia and its quays are perfect for a digestive walk after the meal.</p>
    </div>

